WEBVTT

1
00:45:05.378 --> 00:45:06.378
Hallelujah.

2
00:45:09.738 --> 00:45:10.738
Yes.

3
00:45:16.778 --> 00:45:20.258
Is there anyone in the room who agrees with me when I say that God is good?

4
00:45:21.018 --> 00:45:22.338
Amen. He is good, isn't He?

5
00:45:23.138 --> 00:45:24.138
Free shot.

6
00:45:26.338 --> 00:45:27.538
A few years ago...

7
00:45:28.618 --> 00:45:32.098
Let me put it this way. A few years ago, by now...

8
00:45:32.738 --> 00:45:34.298
That was 2016.

9
00:45:35.298 --> 00:45:39.538
In 2016, I came, together with Vanessa and my parents, to this room...

10
00:45:40.258 --> 00:45:42.818
I came on a Monday morning to pray here.

11
00:45:44.058 --> 00:45:45.058
And...

12
00:45:46.218 --> 00:45:50.458
at that time there was a gap in the church.

13
00:45:51.218 --> 00:45:54.138
There was an age gap in the church.

14
00:45:55.378 --> 00:45:58.378
Raise your hand if you are in the age...

15
00:45:59.618 --> 00:46:02.338
35 to 45.

16
00:46:02.938 --> 00:46:06.098
Yes, this age group was completely absent.

17
00:46:06.618 --> 00:46:07.618
That was really very bizarre.

18
00:46:08.578 --> 00:46:12.418
So my age group was completely absent in the church.

19
00:46:13.338 --> 00:46:14.338
It was a very big gap.

20
00:46:15.458 --> 00:46:16.458
A significant absence.

21
00:46:17.458 --> 00:46:19.458
And that was a prayer point. Do you remember that, Vanessa?

22
00:46:20.218 --> 00:46:21.858
Do you all remember that, Pama? Do you all remember that?

23
00:46:23.898 --> 00:46:25.418
Yes, that was really...

24
00:46:26.298 --> 00:46:27.298
And we were praying for that.

25
00:46:28.538 --> 00:46:30.538
And we just said, here you want to add.

26
00:46:30.578 --> 00:46:35.618
Here you want to add to this congregation, this age category, this age group.

27
00:46:36.898 --> 00:46:37.898
And here they are.

28
00:46:38.418 --> 00:46:43.018
God does what you ask for that is in line with his kingdom.

29
00:46:43.138 --> 00:46:44.738
That is the important thing.

30
00:46:45.218 --> 00:46:47.218
It must be in line with his will.

31
00:46:47.818 --> 00:46:51.418
You can ask for anything. If it is not in his will, it really won't happen.

32
00:46:52.018 --> 00:46:55.858
But if it is in his will, if your will is synchronized with his will...

33
00:46:55.978 --> 00:46:59.098
or to say it the other way around, if his will is synchronized with your will...

34
00:46:59.098 --> 00:47:03.898
then you can ask and he can align the desires of your heart with his will.

35
00:47:04.298 --> 00:47:05.298
And he can do it.

36
00:47:05.698 --> 00:47:08.898
Why am I saying this a few years later, during a men's camp...

37
00:47:10.298 --> 00:47:12.298
I taught a certain sermon.

38
00:47:12.698 --> 00:47:16.098
And that sermon was based on what Paul said to the men...

39
00:47:16.298 --> 00:47:19.898
I want you men to lift up your holy hands.

40
00:47:20.498 --> 00:47:22.898
And pray together and lift up holy hands.

41
00:47:23.098 --> 00:47:24.898
Who among the men can still remember that?

42
00:47:25.898 --> 00:47:26.898
Good job.

43
00:47:30.098 --> 00:47:33.298
And during the worship just now, and I see it more often...

44
00:47:33.498 --> 00:47:36.898
I see men lifting their holy hands to heaven.

45
00:47:37.898 --> 00:47:40.498
Women, you are amazing.

46
00:47:40.898 --> 00:47:42.898
Because women, you are already doing that.

47
00:47:43.498 --> 00:47:46.298
Women are more emotionally open.

48
00:47:47.098 --> 00:47:50.698
And so your worship is often evident.

49
00:47:51.498 --> 00:47:53.698
But men can be closed off.

50
00:47:53.898 --> 00:47:57.898
And this was a situation in the church.

51
00:47:57.898 --> 00:48:01.498
There was truly something going on that men were more closed off.

52
00:48:01.898 --> 00:48:05.098
But I see in the last few years, through prayer...

53
00:48:05.898 --> 00:48:10.298
in this church, I see men lifting their holy hands to heaven.

54
00:48:10.898 --> 00:48:12.298
And this is a good sign.

55
00:48:12.698 --> 00:48:18.498
These are signs of a healthy, spiritual worship culture.

56
00:48:18.698 --> 00:48:23.298
Where men and women, young and old and middle-aged...

57
00:48:23.498 --> 00:48:25.098
fully go for the Lord.

58
00:48:25.298 --> 00:48:27.298
Putting their trust in King Jesus.

59
00:48:27.498 --> 00:48:29.898
And lifting their holy hands to heaven.

60
00:48:30.098 --> 00:48:31.098
I love it.

61
00:48:31.498 --> 00:48:34.898
And it was about a year and a half ago, or a year ago...

62
00:48:35.498 --> 00:48:38.698
that I started to introduce in the church...

63
00:48:38.898 --> 00:48:41.698
at the end of the worship, at the end of the worship...

64
00:48:41.898 --> 00:48:44.498
that I said, instead of, let's shake hands...

65
00:48:44.698 --> 00:48:46.298
and hello, and this and that.

66
00:48:46.898 --> 00:48:49.698
Instead, I started to introduce...

67
00:48:49.898 --> 00:48:54.698
with intention, I want to see the church learn to pray for itself.

68
00:48:55.298 --> 00:48:57.498
And so at the end of the worship, I said...

69
00:48:57.698 --> 00:49:00.698
turn to your left or to your right or to the back or to the front...

70
00:49:00.898 --> 00:49:02.498
and pray together.

71
00:49:02.898 --> 00:49:05.498
Go together and magnify the Lord, with your own words.

72
00:49:05.698 --> 00:49:07.698
Listen to each other and bless each other.

73
00:49:08.098 --> 00:49:09.698
Blessing each other is a good season.

74
00:49:09.898 --> 00:49:12.098
Bless each other when you are in a difficult season.

75
00:49:12.298 --> 00:49:13.698
Pray for each other.

76
00:49:14.098 --> 00:49:15.498
What is the effect of that?

77
00:49:15.698 --> 00:49:19.298
Instead of people from the church coming to the church...

78
00:49:19.498 --> 00:49:22.898
being served the worship on a silver platter...

79
00:49:22.898 --> 00:49:24.698
and oh yes, just let it wash over me.

80
00:49:24.898 --> 00:49:26.698
And the Word, oh yes, just let it wash over me...

81
00:49:26.898 --> 00:49:28.498
and then we passively go home again.

82
00:49:28.698 --> 00:49:31.498
Instead, the church of Jesus Christ must...

83
00:49:31.698 --> 00:49:33.098
be an active church.

84
00:49:33.498 --> 00:49:36.098
And these are all things that Paul writes about...

85
00:49:36.298 --> 00:49:37.898
in Philippians and in Ephesians...

86
00:49:38.098 --> 00:49:41.298
that the believers come together to be equipped...

87
00:49:41.498 --> 00:49:43.898
to be the believers the kingdom of God.

88
00:49:44.098 --> 00:49:46.298
This is the building of the kingdom of God.

89
00:49:46.498 --> 00:49:49.898
And I can just as a pastor,...

90
00:49:49.898 --> 00:49:52.298
I can just say that I am proud...

91
00:49:52.498 --> 00:49:55.298
to see a healthy culture in open church.

92
00:49:55.498 --> 00:49:58.498
I am happy about that and I give God the honor for it in Jesus' name.

93
00:49:58.698 --> 00:49:59.698
Amen.

94
00:49:59.898 --> 00:50:00.898
Amen.

95
00:50:04.498 --> 00:50:06.698
Last week I went with Bram...

96
00:50:06.898 --> 00:50:11.098
to an accounting office in Geldermalsen.

97
00:50:11.298 --> 00:50:13.298
Who knows where Geldermalsen is?

98
00:50:13.898 --> 00:50:16.098
That is the Bible Belt of the Netherlands.

99
00:50:16.298 --> 00:50:17.698
And that is really very nice.

100
00:50:17.898 --> 00:50:21.298
As a church, you have to make sure...

101
00:50:21.498 --> 00:50:26.898
that the administration of the church is above board.

102
00:50:27.098 --> 00:50:28.298
You really need to take care of that.

103
00:50:28.498 --> 00:50:31.498
Why? If the tax authorities come to check you...

104
00:50:31.698 --> 00:50:34.098
if the government comes to see how you are doing...

105
00:50:34.298 --> 00:50:39.298
then you need to ensure that everything is accounted for down to the last receipt...

106
00:50:39.498 --> 00:50:41.498
is above board.

107
00:50:41.698 --> 00:50:42.698
That everything is correct.

108
00:50:42.898 --> 00:50:47.298
Because in society and in the difficult times we live in...

109
00:50:47.298 --> 00:50:49.498
Paul speaks in that way too.

110
00:50:49.698 --> 00:50:52.898
In the time we live in, you need to ensure...

111
00:50:53.098 --> 00:50:56.698
that everything is well organized as the congregation of Jesus Christ.

112
00:50:56.898 --> 00:50:57.898
That it is correct.

113
00:50:58.098 --> 00:51:00.098
That you are a healthy, stable church.

114
00:51:00.298 --> 00:51:05.898
So that Satan cannot find anything to criticize you about.

115
00:51:06.098 --> 00:51:08.098
Because if that were the case...

116
00:51:08.298 --> 00:51:10.498
then there could always be powers and forces...

117
00:51:10.698 --> 00:51:13.498
that would love to tear you down as a church.

118
00:51:13.698 --> 00:51:14.698
Do you understand what I mean?

119
00:51:15.098 --> 00:51:18.298
That is why it is important that Open Church manages everything healthily...

120
00:51:18.498 --> 00:51:21.498
and stable and strong and powerful and healthy.

121
00:51:21.698 --> 00:51:25.698
And so also for our finances and for our tax return...

122
00:51:25.898 --> 00:51:28.498
and all those kinds of things we need to ensure...

123
00:51:28.698 --> 00:51:30.498
that everything is properly arranged.

124
00:51:30.698 --> 00:51:32.698
And for that, we need an accounting firm.

125
00:51:32.898 --> 00:51:34.898
We have amazing people in this church...

126
00:51:35.098 --> 00:51:37.098
who are amazing with Excel.

127
00:51:37.298 --> 00:51:38.298
That is a ministry.

128
00:51:38.498 --> 00:51:41.498
Excel for nerds, of course.

129
00:51:42.298 --> 00:51:46.298
But that is not enough.

130
00:51:46.498 --> 00:51:48.498
We should not arrange that internally.

131
00:51:48.698 --> 00:51:50.898
You should arrange that externally.

132
00:51:51.098 --> 00:51:54.498
So that an accounting firm can have everything arranged.

133
00:51:54.698 --> 00:51:57.098
So that when you need to show everything...

134
00:51:57.298 --> 00:51:59.698
you can show everything with a stamp on it...

135
00:51:59.898 --> 00:52:01.898
from a reliable accounting firm...

136
00:52:02.098 --> 00:52:03.898
to show that everything is well arranged.

137
00:52:04.098 --> 00:52:06.098
You are following me, right?

138
00:52:06.298 --> 00:52:10.298
And now with the construction project, the new construction project...

139
00:52:10.298 --> 00:52:13.298
we have gone to an accounting firm...

140
00:52:13.498 --> 00:52:16.498
anyway to have our annual accounts properly arranged.

141
00:52:16.698 --> 00:52:19.698
This accounting firm is called Van Re.

142
00:52:19.898 --> 00:52:22.298
Van Re, accounting firms, they are located in Gelderland.

143
00:52:22.498 --> 00:52:24.098
They are located all over the country.

144
00:52:24.298 --> 00:52:26.298
It is a wonderful organization...

145
00:52:26.498 --> 00:52:28.498
with a whole lot of Christians.

146
00:52:28.698 --> 00:52:30.298
And do you know how nice that is?

147
00:52:30.498 --> 00:52:32.498
Do you know how nice it is to have had a meeting last Tuesday...

148
00:52:32.698 --> 00:52:34.698
with accountants...

149
00:52:34.898 --> 00:52:36.298
who are also Christians?

150
00:52:36.498 --> 00:52:38.498
Then you have to sit a bit higher up in the country.

151
00:52:38.898 --> 00:52:41.898
Because here in the southern Brabant...

152
00:52:42.098 --> 00:52:43.498
it's like, yes, we are a church.

153
00:52:43.698 --> 00:52:44.698
Yes, what?

154
00:52:44.898 --> 00:52:45.898
Yes, a church.

155
00:52:46.098 --> 00:52:47.098
What?

156
00:52:47.298 --> 00:52:50.298
But if you sit in the Netherlands, sitting higher up...

157
00:52:50.498 --> 00:52:52.498
they don't look at that strangely at all.

158
00:52:52.698 --> 00:52:54.698
On the contrary, they actually engage in conversation with you.

159
00:52:54.898 --> 00:52:57.898
They really say at the end of the conversation...

160
00:52:58.098 --> 00:52:59.098
Amen, brother.

161
00:52:59.298 --> 00:53:00.298
That is just amazing.

162
00:53:00.498 --> 00:53:02.498
That is nice, because that makes for very pleasant conversation.

163
00:53:02.698 --> 00:53:05.698
And so also when you talk about the new construction project...

164
00:53:05.898 --> 00:53:06.898
that we are working on...

165
00:53:07.098 --> 00:53:10.098
and we went for it this past Tuesday...

166
00:53:10.298 --> 00:53:13.298
then you can talk about the finances of Open Church.

167
00:53:13.498 --> 00:53:15.498
You can discuss the history.

168
00:53:15.698 --> 00:53:16.698
We did that.

169
00:53:16.898 --> 00:53:18.898
We discussed the history of the congregation.

170
00:53:19.098 --> 00:53:21.098
We showed the numbers...

171
00:53:21.298 --> 00:53:23.298
showed the savings...

172
00:53:23.498 --> 00:53:25.498
and showed our financing needs.

173
00:53:25.698 --> 00:53:28.698
We simply showed how our entire plan looks.

174
00:53:28.898 --> 00:53:31.898
What I find so cool about that is that these people...

175
00:53:32.098 --> 00:53:35.098
men of God, accountants...

176
00:53:35.298 --> 00:53:38.298
from a very solid and good accounting firm...

177
00:53:38.498 --> 00:53:43.498
gave Open Church a compliment about how we as a church...

178
00:53:43.698 --> 00:53:46.698
One, have our finances in order.

179
00:53:46.898 --> 00:53:48.898
We have saved properly.

180
00:53:49.098 --> 00:53:52.098
And Bram, our treasurer, has ensured...

181
00:53:52.298 --> 00:53:54.298
that everything is neatly arranged.

182
00:53:54.498 --> 00:53:58.498
And even the story we have written for the accounting firm...

183
00:53:58.698 --> 00:54:01.698
to present that to them, to show that...

184
00:54:01.898 --> 00:54:02.898
look, this is us.

185
00:54:02.898 --> 00:54:04.898
They even said as a compliment...

186
00:54:05.098 --> 00:54:07.098
you have done this very well.

187
00:54:07.298 --> 00:54:10.298
And that is also worth an applause for our treasurer.

188
00:54:10.498 --> 00:54:12.498
He is standing back there.

189
00:54:12.698 --> 00:54:14.698
Bram, give a wave.

190
00:54:15.898 --> 00:54:17.898
I think it's super cool.

191
00:54:19.098 --> 00:54:21.098
So we are working on...

192
00:54:21.298 --> 00:54:23.298
in the past year, in 2024...

193
00:54:23.498 --> 00:54:25.498
we have been working on the construction project.

194
00:54:25.698 --> 00:54:29.698
And the first thing we had to do...

195
00:54:29.898 --> 00:54:31.898
the first project we had to do...

196
00:54:31.898 --> 00:54:34.898
is to apply for the permit from the government.

197
00:54:35.098 --> 00:54:38.098
That went remarkably well.

198
00:54:38.298 --> 00:54:41.298
Such a building permit application takes six months.

199
00:54:41.498 --> 00:54:43.498
And on the day after six months...

200
00:54:43.698 --> 00:54:45.698
we literally received the permit.

201
00:54:45.898 --> 00:54:48.898
Without complaints from the government, without complaints from the neighbors.

202
00:54:49.098 --> 00:54:52.098
This is a unique situation, both the architect...

203
00:54:52.298 --> 00:54:55.298
and at the government we have heard multiple times...

204
00:54:55.498 --> 00:54:57.498
that they say this is quite special...

205
00:54:57.698 --> 00:55:00.698
that you have no complaints from anyone at all...

206
00:55:00.698 --> 00:55:03.698
on the stamp date of this is the application...

207
00:55:03.898 --> 00:55:05.898
and on that day you can have it in...

208
00:55:06.098 --> 00:55:08.098
God has indicated a green light here...

209
00:55:08.298 --> 00:55:11.298
and I am very grateful for this to the Lord.

210
00:55:13.498 --> 00:55:15.498
That was 2024.

211
00:55:15.698 --> 00:55:17.698
Now we have entered 2025...

212
00:55:17.898 --> 00:55:20.898
and we have entered the financial side.

213
00:55:21.098 --> 00:55:23.098
Now we are going, I believe...

214
00:55:23.298 --> 00:55:28.298
